      "writtenOn": "2018-05-17T05:04:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So even in S3/S5, you poll the base status to check when it gets disconnected? That might consume some non-negligible amount of power...\n\nOn power_on, can you redo the detection logic instead, to make sure the base is attached? (maybe cutting power and setting state \u003d BASE_DETACHED is enough, so that base_detect_deferred re-detects it?)",
      "revId": "344ec3d70961b2fa5ce3ff09a799581070fe9208",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5e332c0_a076bb22",
        "filename": "board/nocturne/base_detect.c",
