        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-05-17T05:56:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, right, S3/S0ix does not matter here, this is CHIPSET_STARTUP (so boot from S5).\n\nIn S5, you do not poll for disconnection, so you have no idea if state is reliable (it might say BASE_ATTACHED but the base might have been detached while in S5). My concern here is that you are applying power blindly, without knowing if the base is present. We should not apply power to the pogo if the base is not there.",
      "parentUuid": "a5e332c0_a076bb22",
      "revId": "344ec3d70961b2fa5ce3ff09a799581070fe9208",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
